 "notes": "95% exclusion limit on epsilon traced from the black curve of Fig. 9 (epsilonLimitZoom.png in the e-print), the paper's headline observed limit over 50-300 MHz (0.21-1.24 ueV). Axis calibration from tick marks (linear mass axis 0.2-1.2 ueV; log epsilon axis 1e-14 to 1e-12). Paper assumes rho_DM = 0.45 GeV/cm^3, matching the compilation convention, so no rescaling applied. The curve is highly jagged (tracks the shielded-room resonant mode structure); downsampled to ~100 points from ~520 pixel columns, so the narrowest spikes/dips (full range 6e-15 to 6e-13 per abstract) are slightly smoothed. Orange uncertainty band in the figure not traced. Also excluded a single interference candidate (identified as electronics), so the result is a null search.",
